The real problem is that the engine auto-selects the first eligible creature when a cost requires sacrifice, but since Skirsdag Cultist itself is a creature on the battlefield, it could end up sacrificing itself as the cost to activate its own ability—which doesn't make sense. The player needs to choose which creature to sacrifice, and the source creature should probably be excluded from the eligible targets. Looking at the actual implementation, the engine checks whether the player controls at least one creature during action generation, but then during resolution it just grabs the first eligible creature without letting the player choose—which is exactly the bug the TODO comment flags.

The targeting setup looks right for "any target," but I need to verify that damage application actually handles planeswalkers correctly when they're the target. I need to understand how planeswalker damage is actually handled in this engine—whether `damage_marked` is the right approach or if there's special logic elsewhere for loyalty counters. Let me trace through the target generation to see if planeswalkers are even included as valid targets for abilities.

